    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List every shortest path between every pair of nodes.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List every shortest path between every pair of nodes.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n  .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: List every shortest path between every pair of nodes.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nList every shortest path between every pair of nodes.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L61427-L61522){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths(weighted=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![All-pairs all shortest paths](../assets/graphs/all-pairs-all-shortest-paths.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A four-node cycle 1, 2, 3, 4. Between opposite corners there are two equally short routes, such as 1, 2, 3 (accent color) and 1, 4, 3 (teal). The matrix counts the shortest paths for every source and target: 2 for the four opposite pairs (highlighted) and 1 otherwise, 20 paths in total.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nRuns `single_source_all_shortest_paths()` from every node. The output can be very large,\nsince the number of shortest paths grows quickly with graph size; it is meant for small\ngraphs, teaching, and exhaustive checks.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights. If `None` (default), follows the graph's `weighted`\n    flag.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[int, dict[int, list[list[int]]]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `result[source][target]` is the sorted list of shortest paths.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If a negative cycle exists.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nOne predecessor search per source plus path enumeration; matches NetworkX's\n`all_pairs_all_shortest_paths`.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~single_source_all_shortest_paths`) \n\n:   Every shortest path from one source.\n\n[](`~all_pairs_shortest_path`) \n\n:   One shortest path for every pair.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn a square, each node reaches itself and its two neighbors by one path each, and the\nopposite corner by two, so there are 4 x (1 + 2 + 2) = 20 paths in all:\n\n::: {#4b51e7f7 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nsquare = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(4)\neverything = square.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths()\nsum(len(paths) for row in everything.values() for paths in row.values())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n20\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Ties on the metro\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, with each stretch of track weighted by its\ntravel time in minutes. Of the 190 pairs of stations, 42 have more than one fastest route,\nand 16 of these have three:\n\n::: {#f4e8f4fa .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\neverything = metro.all_pairs_all_shortest_paths()\n\nties = {\n    (s, t): routes\n    for s, row in everything.items()\n    for t, routes in row.items()\n    if s < t and len(routes) > 1\n}\ncounts = [len(routes) for routes in ties.values()]\n\nlen(ties), counts.count(3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(42, 16)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nBetween Westgate and University, the three routes go through Central, through Cathedral,\nand over the hills by Hillcrest:\n\n::: {#e9a990c8 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nends = (\"Westgate\", \"University\")\npair = tuple(metro.get_id_from_label(e) for e in ends)\nsteps = [step for route in ties[pair] for step in zip(route, route[1:])]\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", highlight=steps, label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#